{:edb/db-before-t 1849 :edb/db-after-t 1850 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535162 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:21:57.385Z" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119477 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119477 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t)] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle$." 13194139535162 false] [17592186119477 1145 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119477 1145 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2} \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t = \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2} \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}[3f(t) + g(t)]dt &= 3∫_{0}^{2}f(t)dt + ∫_{0}^{2}g(t)dt \\\\\n&= 3⟨16, 2,-2⟩ + ⟨2,-4, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨48, 6,-6⟩ + ⟨2,-4, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨50, 2,-4⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 false] [17592186119478 1100 "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle$." 13194139535162 false] [17592186119478 1100 "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119478 1145 "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{0}f(t)dt &= ∫_{-1}^{1}f(t)dt - ∫_{0}^{1}f(t)dt \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 2, 6⟩ - ⟨\\frac{3}{2}, 1, 3⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - \\frac{3}{2}, 1, 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 false] [17592186119478 1145 "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119479 1100 "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119479 1100 "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1} \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$\nand\n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k$." 13194139535162 false] [17592186119479 1145 "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119479 1145 "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1} \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t = \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1} \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1}c \\cdot f(t)dt &= c \\cdot ∫_{0}^{1}f(t)dt \\\\\n&= (j - k) \\cdot (i - 3j - 4k) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{vmatrix}i -\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{vmatrix}j +\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\\n&= (-4 - 3)i - (0 + 1)j + (0 - 1)k \\\\\n&=-7i - j - k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 false] [17592186119622 1100 "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle$." 13194139535162 false] [17592186119622 1100 "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119622 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}f(t)dt &= - ∫_{2}^{0}f(t)dt \\\\\n&= - ⟨ - 3, 2, 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-2,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{2}f(t) + ⟨1,-1, 1⟩dt &= ∫_{0}^{2}f(t)dt + ∫_{0}^{2}⟨1,-1, 1⟩dt \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-2,-1⟩ + ⟨t,-t, t⟩ \\mid _{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-2,-1⟩ + ⟨2,-2, 2⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨5,-4, 1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 false] [17592186119622 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186119800 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334669 13194139535162 true] [17592186119800 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334676 13194139535162 true] [17592186119800 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334746 13194139535162 true] [17592186119800 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334753 13194139535162 true] [17592186119800 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334760 13194139535162 true] [17592186119905 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334655 13194139535162 true] [17592186119905 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334662 13194139535162 true] [17592186119905 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334725 13194139535162 true] [17592186119905 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334732 13194139535162 true] [17592186119905 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334739 13194139535162 true] [17592186119906 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334683 13194139535162 true] [17592186119906 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334690 13194139535162 true] [17592186119906 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334767 13194139535162 true] [17592186119906 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334774 13194139535162 true] [17592186119907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334697 13194139535162 true] [17592186119907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334704 13194139535162 true] [17592186119907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334711 13194139535162 true] [17592186119907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334718 13194139535162 true] [17592186119907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186334781 13194139535162 true] [17592186120482 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535162 true] [17592186120482 1100 "Calculate\n\n$∫_{1}^{2}f(t)dt$\ngiven that\n$∫_{1}^{3}f(t)dt = ⟨ - 2, 3, 4⟩$\nand\n$∫_{2}^{3}f(t)dt = ⟨8,-6, 15⟩$." 13194139535162 false] [17592186120482 1100 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186120482 1145 "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334655 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334656 13194139535162 true] [17592186334655 1089 "q-129140" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334655 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535162 true] [17592186334655 1100 "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334655 1113 #uuid "3649b2fe-dd3f-5319-9372-b19d8b8dbcb0" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334655 1145 "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,-6,\\,3⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334657 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334658 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334659 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334660 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334661 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1041 "selection" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334660 13194139535162 true] [17592186334656 1110 #uuid "800c3d62-349a-536b-adb9-bebc3271fe2b" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334657 1034 "⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-6,\\,1⟩" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535162 true] [17592186334657 1111 #uuid "6ef1d1af-4db6-5b3b-9d5d-960b80e29691" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334658 1034 "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-5,\\,2⟩" 13194139535162 true] [17592186334658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941395